NUM-26: count an on-sag inlet's street sides after loading its geometry

getOnSagCapturedFlow() formed totalInlets = Nsides * numInlets before
getConduitGeometry() set the file-scope Nsides for this inlet, so an on-sag
inlet was scaled by the street sides of the inlet processed before it: a sag
inlet on a half street captured twice its flow after a full-street inlet,
and a full-street sag inlet half after a half-street one. Compute
totalInlets after the geometry call.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-26_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
index fa52cb3..0b65ddf 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
@@ -1584,12 +1584,12 @@ double getOnSagCapturedFlow(TInlet* inlet, double q, double d)
     double qCaptured = 0.0, qMax = BIG;
 
     if (inlet->numInlets == 0) return 0.0;
-    totalInlets = Nsides * inlet->numInlets;
     linkIndex = inlet->linkIndex;
     designIndex = inlet->designIndex;
 
     // --- store conduit geometry in shared variables
     getConduitGeometry(inlet);
+    totalInlets = Nsides * inlet->numInlets;
 
     // --- set flow limit per inlet
     if (inlet->flowLimit > 0.0)
